[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m 1. Convert \(17_b\) to base 10:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m \[ 17_b = 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m 2. Convert \(97_b\) to base 10:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m \[ 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m We need \(17_b\) to be a divisor of \(97_b\), so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m \[ 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m This means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m for some integer \(k\). Rearranging gives:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = kb + 7k \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m \[ 9b - kb = 7k - 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m \[ b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m \[ b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m Since \(b > 9\), we need to find values of \(k\) such that \(b\) is an integer greater than 9. Let's iterate through possible values of \(k\) to find valid \(b\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m We'll start with \(k = 2\) and go upwards, checking if \(b\) is an integer and greater than 9.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=4038243)[0m 
